Caught your eye? Great. Keep going...

We are Nimber, and we are not just filling positions, we are building a team that is ready to shake things up. If you are ready to rewrite the rules and make a real impact, this is your moment. Join us and lets put the future where it belongs. In the hands of passionate people.

But what does Nimber mean?In mathematics and game theory, they are numbers with special properties of addition and multiplication. And what we really want is to add value to customers' projects.

Position:

Location:
Oporto - Hybrid

Job Summary
: The role is focused on Production Engineering and Application Support, ensuring the stability, reliability, and continuous improvement of critical applications in production environments. Responsibilities include application analysis and standardization, automation and industrialization of processes, as well as supporting technical and functional evolutions. The role requires a strong focus on operational excellence, automation, and maintaining secure and highly reliable production environments.

Key Responsibilities:

Operational support on all environments (investigate and resolve incident & issues, change requests, maintenance, on call ...);
Level 3 Support on IT infrastructure;
Ensure Stability of applications and systems (Set up relevant monitoring metrics, resilient architecture...);
Drive technical projects with infrastructure and dev teams (drive meetings & planning);
Participate in providing technical architecture and support on Business Projects;
Improve our tools and procedures (shell scripting, PowerShell, test scenario...);
Provide secure architecture, standards (comply with SLAs);
Available 24/7 for maintenances and issues;
Follow-up and coordination of changes and technical operations (electrical shutdown, servers move, etc.);
Change management : production of new versions of applications and any change on infrastructure part;
Carry out the commissioning of the new versions of applications in collaboration with the teams in charge of the development and maintenance of these applications and on the other hand with the technical teams: Systems engineers, Databases, Work and network possibly;
Management of treatment scheduling;
Participate in the resolution of production incidents and contribute in problem management;
Drafting / maj of instructions;
Document the components and operation of applications: software architecture, technical architecture, procedures, supervision needs, ...;
Manage backup data and ensure regular restoring test;
Monitoring application and infrastructure with efficient alerting system to guarantee SLA with business line;
Control load capacity for application and adapt infrastructure ressource by more allcation or redesigning architecture;
Guarantee DRP (Disaster Recovery Plan) : twice test a year to ensure different scenario (like Datacenter lost, server or network failure);
Project management : define technical architecture for new application using infrastructure standards and work with dev team to build it.

Requirements:

Minimum 6 years of experience on Linux IT Project;
Good knowledge of Linux environments (Windows Server is a plus);
Proficiency in scripting languages (shell, phyton);
Strong understanding in web servers (manage migration from websphere to jboss for example);
Good knowledge of security: SSL certificates, reverse proxy, loadbalancing;
General knowledge in scheduler tools (Control-M, VTOM);
General knowledge of monitoring tools (Zabbix, Grafana, ELK);
General knowledge of deployments tools (GIT, Jenkins, XL Deploy, XL Release, Bitbucket, Artifactory, Openshift, Docker).

This is our winning strategy, built on the core principles of impartiality, independence, and fairness at Nimber. The only thing missing is you!

Ready to join us and succeed?

If you're tired of feeling like just a number, send us your application and become a Nimber.

